=== 6: Unset array element with interesting expression
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|Initial array:
|declare -a myarray=([0]="a" [1]="b" [2]="c" [3]="d" [4]="e")
|
|After removing element at index 4:
|declare -a myarray=([0]="a" [1]="b" [2]="c" [3]="d")
|
|After removing element at index 3:
|declare -a myarray=([0]="a" [1]="b" [2]="c")
|

=== 7: Unset array element with negative index
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|Initial array:
|declare -a myarray=([0]="a" [1]="b" [2]="c" [3]="d" [4]="e")
|
|After removing last element (index -1):
|declare -a myarray=([0]="a" [1]="b" [2]="c" [3]="d")
|
|After removing new last element (index -1 again):
|declare -a myarray=([0]="a" [1]="b" [2]="c")
|
|After removing second-to-last element (index -2):
|declare -a myarray=([0]="a" [2]="c")
|

=== 8: Unset array element with negative index out of bounds
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|Initial array:
|declare -a myarray=([0]="a" [1]="b" [2]="c")
|
|After attempting to remove with index -4 (out of bounds):
|declare -a myarray=([0]="a" [1]="b" [2]="c")
|Return code: 0
--- stderr
|bash: line 7: unset: [-4]: bad array subscript

